  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe release gate prebuilds debug and release test targets before running suites.\nIt runs up to four independent lanes together and mixes debug and release lanes.\nIt keeps app, kernel, UI and clippy steps alone.\nApp and kernel contain the import watchdogs.\nEach lane keeps its own numbered log and wall time.\nThe summary reports total wall time and summed lane time as a serial estimate.\nThe gate stops after a failed prebuild and preserves checkout VOID checks.\nThe release lockfile guard accepts unchanged lines whose endings changed between LF and CRLF.\nIt still refuses changed package names and checksums.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe gate ran every step serially.\nThe lockfile guard counted line-ending churn as nonversion changes.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe prebuild and CRLF pins failed before the fixes.\nPins: `release_prebuilds_both_profiles_before_running_suites` and `lock_diff_guard_ignores_only_line_ending_changes`.\nAdditional pins cover four lanes, profile mixing, exactly-once scheduling, isolation and selected runs.\n`release_executor_overlaps_lanes_and_keeps_failure_and_checkout_guards` runs real child commands to check overlap, failure aggregation, failed-build stopping and checkout VOID.\nRestoring upstream plan.rs, exec.rs and release_bump.rs made their pins fail.\nForcing singleton waves and removing the failed-build stop also made their pins fail.\nRestoring each fix made its pin pass.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 136 xtask tests.\n`cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nA warmed Cargo probe with four two-second test runs measured 8.086 seconds serially and 2.052 seconds concurrently.\nCargo released its build lock before executing tests.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe diff contains no changed .nc or .cl files.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA full release-tier serial versus parallel benchmark remains unexercised.\nSummed lane time is an estimate and does not replace that benchmark.\nThis run did not exercise real UI windows or the Windows release command.\nThe CRLF regression uses a text fixture.\nThe optional split across uma and m3 is deferred.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone among open PRs for the changed files.\nThis branch starts at upstream/main commit 085a4717.\n\nEffort: high\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: Run independent release-gate lanes up to four at a time and accept CRLF-only Cargo.lock changes during release validation.\n\nFixes #1703\n",
